  "scope": "A supplied unitary symbol map preserves the complete free determinant while a new pointwise positive quartic interaction has uniformly localized field packets and an exact finite cubature. The first coupling derivative is a volume term plus the homogeneous Einstein curvature functional with a bounded remainder. Convexity bounds the finite-coupling Taylor error per volume, not per curvature scale. No independent local site algebra, microscopic refinement law, arbitrary-metric finite-coupling Einstein action, Lorentzian gravity, Standard Model, or TOE is proved. No new Lean theorem."
}
